-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 65: SIMPLIFIED PROCESS FOR PROCEEDINGS IN MAGISTRATE'S COURT OR DISTRICT COURT (part roc12, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the thing holds as the Order states it.
--   JUST FALSE   the Order says no in its own words (a flat negative, a closed "only" list, a "where" or "if"
--                condition not met, a period or limit the text fixes).
--   NOTHING      the Order does not answer: it is silent, it limits a grant by its own wording, a bare "must"
--                has not been done, or the answer lives in a provision outside this Order.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every answer carries the caveat of O 3 r 2(1) (the Court's discretion to order otherwise); no function threads it.


-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 65 -- Simplified process in the Magistrate's Court or the District Court`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- application of the Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7492 | (2) Where any civil proceedings are before a District Court, and all parties to those proceedings file their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings, this Order, upon the filing of that consent, applies to those proceedings.
@ref O 65 r 1(2) (src:7492)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil proceedings before a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 1(2) this Order applies on the filing of the consent` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are civil proceedings before a District Court` AND `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any civil proceedings are before a District Court, and all parties to those proceedings file their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings, this Order, upon the filing of that consent, applies to those proceedings"

-- src:7485 | 1. —(1) This Order applies only to — ( a )
-- src:7486 | all civil proceedings begun by way of an originating claim which are before a Magistrate’s Court; and
-- src:7487 | ( b )
-- src:7488 | any civil proceedings begun by originating claim — (i)
-- src:7489 | which are before a District Court; and
-- src:7490 | (ii)
-- src:7491 | to which paragraph (2) applies.
@ref O 65 r 1(1) (src:7485-7491)
GIVEN `the document that began the proceedings` IS A `Document kind`
      `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court before which the proceedings are` IS A `Court level`
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 1 r 3(1) a document is an originating claim` `the document that began the proceedings` `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the document is an originating claim depends on Order 6, Rule 5, in another part's range
    WHEN JUST byClaim THEN
        BRANCH
            IF byClaim AND `the court before which the proceedings are` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            IF byClaim AND `o 65 r 1(2) this Order applies on the filing of the consent` (`the court before which the proceedings are` EQUALS `District Court`) `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Order applies only to"

-- src:7493 | (3) Except as otherwise provided in this Order, all the other Orders in these Rules continue to apply to proceedings to which this Order applies.
@ref O 65 r 1(3) (src:7493)
GIVEN `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `this Order provides otherwise for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 1(3) the other Orders continue to apply to the matter` MEANS
    IF `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `this Order provides otherwise for the matter`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as otherwise provided in this Order, all the other Orders in these Rules continue to apply"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to proceedings to which this Order applies"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- upfront production`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7495 | 2. —(1) Every pleading served by a party in a matter to which this Order applies must be accompanied by a list of and a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1). (2) A copy of any document may be in paper form or in an electronic format in a common format that the other party can use.
@ref O 65 r 2(1) (src:7495)
GIVEN `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pleading is accompanied by a list of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pleading is accompanied by a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF    `the pleading is accompanied by a list of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)`
          AND `the pleading is accompanied by a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be accompanied by"; paragraph (4) says a party must not rely on a document not produced in accordance with the Order
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a matter to which this Order applies"

@ref O 65 r 2(2) (src:7495)
GIVEN `the copy is in paper form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is in an electronic format in a common format that the other party can use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 2(2) the copy may be in this form` MEANS
    IF `the copy is in paper form` OR `the copy is in an electronic format in a common format that the other party can use`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): a permission naming two forms ("paper form or in an electronic format in a common format that the other party can use"); it does not forbid others

-- src:7496 | (3) This Rule applies to any amended pleading filed and served by any party if the amended pleading — ( a )
-- src:7497 | pleads any additional fact; or
-- src:7498 | ( b )
-- src:7499 | refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by that party,
-- src:7500 | except that documents previously disclosed in the same proceedings need not be disclosed by reason only of the amendments to the pleadings.
@ref O 65 r 2(3) (src:7496-7500)
GIVEN `the amended pleading is filed and served by a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amended pleading pleads any additional fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amended pleading refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by that party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 2(3) this Rule applies to the amended pleading` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the amended pleading is filed and served by a party`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any amended pleading filed and served by any party"
    ELSE IF `the amended pleading pleads any additional fact` OR `the amended pleading refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by that party`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the amended pleading — (a) pleads any additional fact; or (b) refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by that party"

@ref O 65 r 2(3) (src:7496-7500)
GIVEN `the document was previously disclosed in the same proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 2(3) a previously disclosed document needs to be disclosed by reason only of the amendments` MEANS
    IF `the document was previously disclosed in the same proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "documents previously disclosed in the same proceedings need not be disclosed by reason only of the amendments to the pleadings"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the exception speaks only of documents previously disclosed in the same proceedings

-- src:7501 | (4) In any case to which this Order applies, the parties must not, except as may otherwise be ordered or permitted by the Court, rely on any document that was not produced in accordance with this Order.
@ref O 65 r 2(4) (src:7501)
GIVEN `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 2(4) the party may rely on the document` MEANS
    IF `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `the document was produced in accordance with this Order`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar speaks only of "any document that was not produced in accordance with this Order"; it grants no right to rely
        ELSE IF `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except as may otherwise be ordered or permitted by the Court" lifts the bar and grants nothing (QA default)
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the parties must not, except as may otherwise be ordered or permitted by the Court, rely on any document that was not produced in accordance with this Order"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case to which this Order applies"

@ref O 65 r 2(4) (src:7501)
GIVEN `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 2(4) reliance on the document is barred` MEANS
    IF `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` OR `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is on reliance on a document "not produced in accordance with this Order", "except as may otherwise be ordered or permitted by the Court"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case to which this Order applies"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- excluded interim applications`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 65 r 3 kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 9, Rule 17`
    `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 9, Rule 19`
    `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 11`
    `o 65 r 3 any other application`

-- src:7503 | 3. Without affecting the Court’s powers under Order 9, no application under Order 9, Rule 17 or 19 or Order 11 may be made in any case to which this Order applies.
@ref O 65 r 3 (src:7503)
GIVEN `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `o 65 r 3 kind of application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 3 the application may be made` MEANS
    IF `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 9, Rule 17` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no application under Order 9, Rule 17 or 19 or Order 11 may be made in any case to which this Order applies"
        WHEN `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 9, Rule 19` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no application under Order 9, Rule 17 or 19 or Order 11 may be made in any case to which this Order applies"
        WHEN `o 65 r 3 an application under Order 11` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no application under Order 9, Rule 17 or 19 or Order 11 may be made in any case to which this Order applies"
        WHEN `o 65 r 3 any other application` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rule names only applications under Order 9, Rule 17 or 19 or Order 11
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case to which this Order applies"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- simplified trial`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 65 r 4(1) mode of trial` IS ONE OF
    `o 65 r 4(1)(a) a simplified trial under this Rule`
    `o 65 r 4(1)(b) a full trial to which the provisions of Order 15 apply`
    `o 65 r 4(1) another mode of trial`

-- src:7505 | 4. —(1) If the Court is satisfied that the parties to a case are unable to resolve their dispute without a trial, the Court must as soon as practicable direct that the case be set down for such of the following as the Court deems fit: ( a )
-- src:7506 | a simplified trial under this Rule;
-- src:7507 | ( b )
-- src:7508 | a full trial to which the provisions of Order 15 apply.
@ref O 65 r 4(1) (src:7505-7508)
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied that the parties to the case are unable to resolve their dispute without a trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 4(1) the duty to direct that the case be set down for trial arises` MEANS
    IF `the Court is satisfied that the parties to the case are unable to resolve their dispute without a trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Court is satisfied that the parties to a case are unable to resolve their dispute without a trial"

@ref O 65 r 4(1)(a) and (b) (src:7505-7508)
GIVEN mode IS A `o 65 r 4(1) mode of trial`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 4(1) the mode of trial is one the Rule names` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(1)(a) a simplified trial under this Rule` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(1)(b) a full trial to which the provisions of Order 15 apply` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(1) another mode of trial` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the Court sets the case down "for such of the following as the Court deems fit"; the text does not say that no other mode may be directed

DECLARE `o 65 r 4(2) matter the Court may have regard to` IS ONE OF
    `o 65 r 4(2)(a) the number of parties involved`
    `o 65 r 4(2)(b) the complexity of the issues`
    `o 65 r 4(2)(c) the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any`
    `o 65 r 4(2)(d) whether the costs which may be incurred will be proportionate to the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any`
    `o 65 r 4(2)(e) the nature of the action`
    `o 65 r 4(2)(f) any other matter`

-- src:7509 | (2) In deciding the appropriate mode of trial, the Court may have regard to the following matters: ( a )
-- src:7510 | the number of parties involved;
-- src:7511 | ( b )
-- src:7512 | the complexity of the issues;
-- src:7513 | ( c )
-- src:7514 | the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any;
-- src:7515 | ( d )
-- src:7516 | whether the costs which may be incurred will be proportionate to the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any;
-- src:7517 | ( e )
-- src:7518 | the nature of the action;
-- src:7519 | ( f )
-- src:7520 | any other matter that the Court considers relevant.
@ref O 65 r 4(2) (src:7509-7520)
GIVEN matter IS A `o 65 r 4(2) matter the Court may have regard to`
      `the Court considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 4(2) the Court may have regard to the matter in deciding the mode of trial` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(2)(a) the number of parties involved` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(2)(b) the complexity of the issues` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(2)(c) the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(2)(d) whether the costs which may be incurred will be proportionate to the amount of the claim and the amount of the counterclaim, if any` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(2)(e) the nature of the action` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(2)(f) any other matter` THEN
        IF `the Court considers the matter relevant`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other matter that the Court considers relevant"

DECLARE `o 65 r 4(3) stage of the simplified trial` IS ONE OF
    `o 65 r 4(3)(a) the examination in chief of a witness`
    `o 65 r 4(3)(b) the cross-examination of a witness`
    `o 65 r 4(3)(c) the re-examination of a witness`
    `o 65 r 4(3)(d) the closing submissions of a party`

-- src:7521 | (3) The conduct of a simplified trial is governed by Order 15, but the following time limits apply: ( a )
-- src:7522 | for the examination in chief of a witness — 10 minutes per witness;
-- src:7523 | ( b )
-- src:7524 | for the cross‑examination of a witness — 60 minutes per witness;
-- src:7525 | ( c )
-- src:7526 | for the re‑examination of a witness — 10 minutes per witness;
-- src:7527 | ( d )
-- src:7528 | for closing submissions — 30 minutes per party.
@ref O 65 r 4(3) (src:7521-7528)
GIVEN stage IS A `o 65 r 4(3) stage of the simplified trial`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 65 r 4(3) the time limit in minutes` MEANS
    CONSIDER stage
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(3)(a) the examination in chief of a witness` THEN 10
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(3)(b) the cross-examination of a witness` THEN 60
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(3)(c) the re-examination of a witness` THEN 10
    WHEN `o 65 r 4(3)(d) the closing submissions of a party` THEN 30

@ref O 65 r 4(3) (src:7521-7528)
GIVEN stage IS A `o 65 r 4(3) stage of the simplified trial`
      `the minutes taken, per witness or per party` IS A NUMBER
      `the time limit as extended by the Court under paragraph (4), if the Court extended it` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time limit as extended by the Court under paragraph (4), if the Court extended it`
    WHEN JUST extended THEN
        IF `the minutes taken, per witness or per party` AT MOST extended
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following time limits apply" (the limit as the Court extended it under paragraph (4))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the minutes taken, per witness or per party` AT MOST `o 65 r 4(3) the time limit in minutes` stage
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following time limits apply: (a) for the examination in chief of a witness — 10 minutes per witness; (b) for the cross-examination of a witness — 60 minutes per witness; (c) for the re-examination of a witness — 10 minutes per witness; (d) for closing submissions — 30 minutes per party"

-- src:7529 | (4) The Court may extend any time limit under paragraph (3) as the Court deems fit.
@ref O 65 r 4(4) (src:7529)
GIVEN `the time limit is one under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 4(4) the Court may extend the time limit` MEANS
    IF `the time limit is one under paragraph (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any time limit under paragraph (3)"

-- src:7530 | (5) In every case to which this Order applies, where judgment has been entered for damages to be assessed, this Rule applies, with the necessary modifications, to the assessment of damages.
@ref O 65 r 4(5) (src:7530)
GIVEN `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `judgment has been entered for damages to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 65 r 4(5) this Rule applies to the assessment of damages` MEANS
    IF `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN
        IF `judgment has been entered for damages to be assessed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where judgment has been entered for damages to be assessed, this Rule applies, with the necessary modifications, to the assessment of damages"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In every case to which this Order applies"

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 65 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names the actor and states no number of days for these duties; "as soon as practicable" in r 4(1) is not a number.

DECLARE `o 65 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 65 a party serving a pleading`
    `o 65 a party in a case to which this Order applies`
    `o 65 the Court`

DECLARE `o 65 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 65 serve the list and the copy of the documents with the pleading`
    `o 65 rely on a document not produced in accordance with this Order`
    `o 65 direct that the case be set down for trial`

-- src:7495 | 2. —(1) Every pleading served by a party in a matter to which this Order applies must be accompanied by a list of and a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1). (2) A copy of any document may be in paper form or in an electronic format in a common format that the other party can use.
@ref O 65 r 2(1) (src:7495)
`o 65 r 2(1) the duty of a party serving a pleading` MEANS
    PARTY `o 65 a party serving a pleading`
    MUST `o 65 serve the list and the copy of the documents with the pleading`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 65 a party serving a pleading` BECAUSE "the pleading was not accompanied by a list of and a copy of all documents falling within the categories in Order 11, Rule 2(1)"

-- src:7501 | (4) In any case to which this Order applies, the parties must not, except as may otherwise be ordered or permitted by the Court, rely on any document that was not produced in accordance with this Order.
@ref O 65 r 2(4) (src:7501)
`o 65 r 2(4) the prohibition on relying on a document not produced` MEANS
    PARTY `o 65 a party in a case to which this Order applies`
    SHANT `o 65 rely on a document not produced in accordance with this Order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 65 a party in a case to which this Order applies` BECAUSE "the party relied on a document that was not produced in accordance with this Order"

-- src:7505 | 4. —(1) If the Court is satisfied that the parties to a case are unable to resolve their dispute without a trial, the Court must as soon as practicable direct that the case be set down for such of the following as the Court deems fit: ( a )
-- src:7506 | a simplified trial under this Rule;
-- src:7507 | ( b )
-- src:7508 | a full trial to which the provisions of Order 15 apply.
@ref O 65 r 4(1) (src:7505-7508)
`o 65 r 4(1) the Court's duty to direct the mode of trial` MEANS
    PARTY `o 65 the Court`
    MUST `o 65 direct that the case be set down for trial`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 65 the Court` BECAUSE "the Court did not direct that the case be set down for a simplified trial or a full trial"
